  "raw_text": "actors, such as taste, portion size, speed, nutrition, consistency, or price, and explain how you judge if something is \"worth it\"? User: Portion size. It's all about portion size when it comes to fast food. I want to be able to get a quality amount of food because I know that your restaurant produces quality food. Besides quantity, if I get rewards for purchasing at the restaurant, I consider that value. Agent: That's very clear. Now, compared to your last fast-food order, what changed today, if anything? Please pick the biggest driver and explain it, whether it was your mood, cravings, schedule, budget, health goals, social plans, or convenience. User: No change. If I can get a bunch of food for $20, I'm there. Agent: Okay, I understand that consistency in value is a key driver for you. So, what \"mode\" are you in today? Are you in a budget, health, treat, convenience, explore, or stressed mode? User: Normal mode trying to fill up my stomach without breaking the bank. Agent: Understoo",
